        "original_id": "38924b51-97a7-57f9-bf8c-f666c712e628",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Tom Kristensen, Petter Solberg, David Coulthard, Pascal Wehrlein, Hamble James Leacock\n- Events: 2014 Race of Champions, Nations' Cup, individual contest, 24 Hours of Le Mans\n- Places: Bushy Park, Barbados\n\nFacts:\n- From 2000 to 2005, Tom Kristensen won six consecutive 24 Hours of Le Mans races.\n- Tom Kristensen holds the record for the most 24 Hours of Le Mans wins with nine.\n- Later in 2014, Bushy Park in Barbados hosted the 2014 Race of Champions.\n- At the 2014 Race of Champions, the Nordic team of Tom Kristensen and Petter Solberg won the Nations' Cup.\n- At the 2014 Race of Champions, David Coulthard won the individual contest by defeating Pascal Wehrlein 2–0 in the final.\n- Hamble James Leacock was born in Barbados, where his father was a slaveholder.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
